r liam finds the drugs  and ingests some debbie finds liam  unconscious in the other room and calls  fiona for help but it seems like it's  too late the young boy is passed out  with white powder all over his face the  paramedics are called and fiona is  arrested for child abuse and possession  of an illegal substance liam ends up  recovering from the overdose but doctors  warn he may experience learning  disabilities moving forward although  this kind of thing isn't completely  unexpected in the series it still  doesn't make it any easier to witness  many viewers felt that this depiction of  child abuse and endangerment was too  much even for a show like shameless  fiona's mistakes didn't start at  disrespecting her dead mother and stop  at endangering her little brother over  the course of the series 11 seasons nine  of which fiona actress emmy rossum  starred in she did a lot of questionable  things and fans had no problem airing  their grievances about the character one  reddit user admitted that he likes  shameless but finds the gallagher family  terrible particularly fiona for a number  of reasons the redditer wrote fiona is  ridiculous she's cheated on pretty much  all of her boyfriends and is controlling  of everyone around her the only thing  she did that could be considered good is  raising her siblings and even then she  has to lord it over anyone who will  listen and she never seems to show  remorse for what she does  i'm not  just chaos  another viewer and redditer pointed out  that when rossum left shameless it  brought fiona's core storyline to an end  at the perfect moment fiona left at the  right place and the right time in my  opinion her role as acting guardian was  more or less fulfilled by the time she  asks ian for permission to leave it's  strikingly obvious that she is no longer  needed not all shameless fans feel this  way of course even in the face of all  fiona has done wrong plenty of viewers  still think she deserves a lot of credit  for